Z||000029||Gold-86SE||05-15-2000||10:44 AM||||<BR>OK guys, you want cruisin' music, how about this.  Since, I can't break it down to just five songs, I'll give you five BEST BANDS, with my favorite albums from each band.<P>THE CULT - (Electric, Sonic Temple, Ceremony, High Octane Cult)<P>MEGADETH - (Countdown to Extinction, Cryptic Writings, Youthanasia, Risk)<P>CCR - (Chronicle I and II)<P>AC/DC (Back In Black, High Voltage, Highway To He!!)<P>Zepplin - (Zep II, III, IV, - ahh what do I mean - anything Zep).<P>CINDERELLA - (Night Songs, Long Cold Winter, Heart Break Station - had to add these guys for extra messure, and for those extra miles)<P>Wilburt, goods sounds, I really like the Vaughn Brothers and Jeff Healey.<P>80's BOY, I love the 80's would not change it for anything, not a better decade to grown up in, except for maybe the 20's or 50's. <BR>(Don't care that I am a bit biased for the 80's, since that was my teenage years).  Seems to me the 80's are like the 50's, nothing but a good time, and fond memories.<P>Additionally, tight curves and fast cars, deserve and need fast music, you certainly don't hear Top 40 or Country Music in Days of Thunder and other great car movies.<P>Laters.<BR>||||reg||6
